  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Agricultural value chain analysis</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Burkina Faso, the rural sector plays a major role in the national economy. It employs around 80% of the total population which contributes to national food and nutritional security. Burkina Faso is considered a &quot;country with an agricultural vocation&quot;. It mainly produces vegetables, cereals, fruits, as well as a variety of livestock.The products have good potential for local and regional markets. The Netherlands embassy in Ouagadougou, Burkina Faso, operates a value chain study to identify ongoing projects and programmes involving Burkina Faso, mode and areas of interventions, identify the promising subsectors and define concrete opportunities for a community led agriculture programme.The findings and recommendations, identified by the study, will contribute to the development of the Netherlands embassy&apos;s strategy on Food and Nutrition and Private Sector Development.</narrative>
  </description>
